WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.715 --> 00:00:10.093
It is time for me to scoop leaves. Would you like to help?

00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:11.177
Sure!

00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:13.346
I like a clean pond. 

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:15.724
(Scoops leaves) And so do the fish!

00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:42.167
Hey there! My name is Jessica Skye and I’m super excited for what we have planned today.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:47.088
But first, let’s pause for a second. Can you hear my windchimes? 

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.724
(Deep inhale - exhale) I love listening to that sound.

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:03.354
It always makes me feel happy and calm, and so many interesting things can happen 

00:01:03.354 --> 00:01:10.236
when we just pay attention to what is happening around us, and inside us, like with our breath.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.237
Let’s try it together.

00:01:12.197 --> 00:01:16.701
Remember that mat or towel you grabbed earlier? It’s time to roll it out on the floor.

00:01:18.328 --> 00:01:21.623
Free to move your pillow if you need to. 

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:31.758
And it’s fine if you don’t have a mat or towel, just find a safe flat surface. 

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:34.010
Now, have a seat and get comfortable. 

00:01:34.552 --> 00:01:42.811
We’re gonna take three nice long breaths, in through the nose and out through the mouth. 

00:01:50.693 --> 00:02:00.370
Two more, and do it with me, inhaling (inhales), exhaling (exhales).

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:12.841
Last one, deep breath in, through your nose, heavy exhale through your mouth.

00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:14.592
What are you doing?

00:02:14.592 --> 00:02:21.307
Stillwater says if you have an angry feeling inside you, sit still, close your eyes, 

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:24.144
and take deep, slow breaths

00:02:27.063 --> 00:02:28.189
It can make you feel better. 

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:36.030
Great job! Now, breathing is one of those things that we do all the time 

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:39.284
and sometimes we don’t even notice it.

00:02:39.284 --> 00:02:43.121
But, if you’re not feeling great on the inside,

00:02:43.621 --> 00:02:47.041
taking a moment to catch your breath can change that,

00:02:47.041 --> 00:02:49.627
and can really help you feel calm. 

00:02:49.627 --> 00:02:51.296
Is it working?

00:02:51.754 --> 00:02:55.925
Actually, it is. (exhales) hhaah…

00:02:55.925 --> 00:03:01.806
Are you ready to try something new? It’s called “deep belly breathing,” 

00:03:01.806 --> 00:03:04.726
and it’s one Stillwater’s favorites.

00:03:05.226 --> 00:03:06.686
I like your big belly!

00:03:07.478 --> 00:03:08.479
Me too!

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:12.817
I’d like you to put one hand, right here, on the top of your stomach, 

00:03:12.942 --> 00:03:13.902
just below your ribs.

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:18.489
And, when you breathe in, do it through your nose, 

00:03:18.573 --> 00:03:23.870
and I want you to try and make your belly big and full.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:27.832
It’s like a balloon, and we’re filling it up with air,

00:03:27.832 --> 00:03:34.839
and when it’s full, go ahead, and exhale super slowly through your mouth. 

00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:37.926
Let me show you and then let’s do it together. 

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:48.478
Ready? Do this one with me 

00:03:59.113 --> 00:04:04.535
Feels good, right? Let’s do it a few more times together. Just keep going. 
&nbsp;

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:15.046
Super calming. One more. 

00:04:24.305 --> 00:04:26.099
Nice job filling up that balloon!

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:28.893
Very nice! I think you’re a natural! 

00:04:29.143 --> 00:04:37.277
Next, I’d like to ask what are some of the things you notice when everything is super quiet?

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:41.531
There are many different ways to be mindful in the world around you. 

00:04:42.198 --> 00:04:45.451
Let’s sit for a moment and just listen. 

00:04:46.327 --> 00:04:50.999
And I find sometimes it helps me focus if I close my eyes.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:52.792
So, give it a go.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:56.212
Soften your gaze, or completely close your eyes, 

00:04:57.213 --> 00:05:00.008
and just tune in with all those noises around you. 
&nbsp;

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:11.477
I can hear the water trickling behind me. 

00:05:15.231 --> 00:05:18.776
I can hear the birds chirping in the distance.

00:05:24.115 --> 00:05:26.784
And the leaves rustling in the wind. 

00:05:31.789 --> 00:05:32.790
What can you hear? 

00:05:35.793 --> 00:05:39.922
Maybe there is a fan, blowing air in the background? 

00:05:41.799 --> 00:05:43.051
A car outside? 

00:05:45.595 --> 00:05:48.639
Maybe your family, in the other room, you can hear them.

00:05:51.351 --> 00:05:58.191
Take a moment. Notice if you can hear your own breath. 

00:06:06.741 --> 00:06:09.118
Isn’t wonderful? 

00:06:09.118 --> 00:06:12.038
Now, let’s use our eyes this time. 

00:06:12.288 --> 00:06:13.289
Where do we start?

00:06:13.623 --> 00:06:19.420
First, start with what you see. The shape of the fruit. The colors.

00:06:19.921 --> 00:06:21.130
So, have a look around. 

00:06:23.633 --> 00:06:27.637
I can see pink flowers. 

00:06:29.138 --> 00:06:32.266
I can see green leaves starting to turn yellow. 

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:38.689
I can see a red table. 

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:44.237
What colors can you find around you, in your space? 

00:06:50.118 --> 00:06:51.661
What colors are the walls?

00:06:54.122 --> 00:06:59.085
Maybe there’s an object on a desk, or a table? What color is that?

00:07:00.711 --> 00:07:03.548
Maybe even look outside your window.

00:07:03.631 --> 00:07:05.258
Notice what you can see there. 

00:07:06.175 --> 00:07:09.095
There are so many colors in the world. 

00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:12.723
So, take a moment, taking them all in. 

00:07:20.481 --> 00:07:22.567
Excellent job using your senses!

00:07:23.526 --> 00:07:25.695
Now, let’s move on to something new! 

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:29.574
Go ahead and stand up on your mat or towel, just like this 

00:07:30.741 --> 00:07:35.204
If you’ve got shoes or socks on, go ahead and take them off now.

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:37.707
We’re gonna give our toes something to do.

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:45.256
All set? Let’s scrunch our toes up and notice what we feel.

00:07:47.842 --> 00:07:51.596
I can feel tingles on the tips of my toes.

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:54.015
What can you feel beneath your toes?

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:55.641
Is it soft?

00:07:56.893 --> 00:08:00.688
Is…anything bunching out between your toes?

00:08:01.522 --> 00:08:04.942
Maybe you’re on wooden floors, or tile?

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:08.029
Is it cold? Is it warm?

00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:13.367
Now, let’s move up from our feet to the rest of our body.

00:08:13.367 --> 00:08:15.328
Do you feel the air around you?

00:08:16.204 --> 00:08:19.499
Maybe there is a fan or a heater?

00:08:19.499 --> 00:08:22.043
And you can feel it blowing air onto your skin.

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:26.380
Or maybe you stood near an open window, and you can feel the breeze coming in.

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:29.133
Did you feel the cold on your back?

00:08:29.133 --> 00:08:30.676
That’s my favorite part!

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:35.223
Perhaps the air in your room is still.

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:38.809
Try moving your arms slowly around you. 

00:08:42.188 --> 00:08:46.651
I bet you can feel the air now. Just notice how that feels.

00:08:47.777 --> 00:08:50.238
It’s like the air is moving out of your way. 

00:08:52.198 --> 00:08:55.493
Just like ripples on a pond. 

00:08:56.869 --> 00:08:59.205
Alright, let’s do one more type of breathing,

00:08:59.205 --> 00:09:02.583
and this is a fun one! It’s called “bee breath.”

00:09:02.583 --> 00:09:04.544
That does sound like fun!

00:09:04.544 --> 00:09:07.129
You know how bees make a buzzing sound?

00:09:07.838 --> 00:09:10.466
That’s where this breathing gets its name from. 

00:09:11.092 --> 00:09:13.302
We’re gonna buzz together like little bees.

00:09:13.928 --> 00:09:17.848
So, let’s take a slow breath in, through our nose,

00:09:18.099 --> 00:09:21.644
and then this time exhale with the mouth closed,

00:09:21.644 --> 00:09:25.022
and make a humming sound. Let me show you first.

00:09:35.992 --> 00:09:38.202
Let’s try it together! Ready?

00:09:50.881 --> 00:09:53.926
Feel how your lips vibrate a little bit and it kinda tickles?

00:09:54.385 --> 00:09:57.722
You can even put one hand on your belly, like before,

00:09:57.722 --> 00:09:59.807
and I bet it’s getting smaller while you’re humming.

00:09:59.807 --> 00:10:01.517
Let’s try it one more time. 

00:10:10.318 --> 00:10:11.319
That’s good!

00:10:11.319 --> 00:10:14.113
Now, I love how this makes me feel!

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:18.075
It relaxes me, and it also energizes me. 

00:10:19.076 --> 00:10:20.202
How does it make you feel?

00:10:20.453 --> 00:10:23.914
How does your face, and tummy, and chest feel now?

00:10:24.165 --> 00:10:27.335
It’s always important to notice how you’re feeling.

00:10:27.835 --> 00:10:30.713
Both on the inside and the outside.

00:10:31.422 --> 00:10:34.884
And, if you’re feeling happy on the inside, that’s wonderful!

00:10:35.801 --> 00:10:38.721
And, if you’re not, that’s okay.

00:10:39.305 --> 00:10:45.770
But, if you take a moment to breathe, it can make you feel a whole lot better!

00:10:45.811 --> 00:10:50.149
Isn’t interesting how these feelings change when you give them time?

00:10:50.149 --> 00:10:53.569
Thank you so much for sharing this part of your day with me.

00:10:54.403 --> 00:10:55.404
See you!

